; ============================================================
; TITLE:    Cesaro Torn Square
; CATEGORY: Fractals
; LEVEL:    Intermediate
; TAGS:     recursion, Cesaro fractal, Koch variant, trigonometry
; SUMMARY:  Tears thin cracks into the sides of a square with Cesaro's sharp version of the Koch curve.
; ============================================================
;
; WHAT IT DOES
;   The Cesaro curve is a Koch curve whose tent is almost closed:
;   the turtle turns 85 degrees instead of 60. Four of these curves
;   make a square whose sides are full of sharp cracks that branch
;   like frost on a window.
;
; HOW TO USE
;   Press Run. Change :angle near the bottom. 60 gives the ordinary
;   Koch curve, numbers near 90 give deeper and thinner cracks.
;
; CONCEPTS YOU WILL LEARN
;   * computing the shrink factor with COS so the curve fits exactly
;   * using one global variable (:angle) inside a recursive procedure
;   * why the bumps point inward when walking clockwise with RIGHT
;     turns on the outside
;
; THINGS TO TRY
;   * Set :angle to 60, 70, 80 and 89 and compare.
;   * Walk the square counterclockwise so the cracks point outward.
;   * Fill the square with FILLED, using a light color.
; ============================================================

; CRACK draws one Cesaro curve. The four pieces are equal; the middle
; two lean in to form the narrow crack.
to crack :len :level
  if :level = 0 [forward :len stop]
  ; With legs of length s and a tent angle A, the whole curve is
  ; s + 2 s cos A + s long. So s = len / (2 + 2 cos A).
  localmake "s :len / (2 + 2 * cos :angle)
  crack :s :level - 1
  right :angle
  crack :s :level - 1
  left 2 * :angle
  crack :s :level - 1
  right :angle
  crack :s :level - 1
end

; TORN.SQUARE walks clockwise around a square. The cracks bend to the
; right of the turtle, which is the inside of the square.
to torn.square :side :level
  penup setxy minus :side / 2 minus :side / 2 setheading 0 pendown
  repeat 4 [crack :side :level right 90]
end

clearscreen hideturtle
setbackground [235 242 250]
make "angle 85
setpencolor [30 70 140]
setpensize 1.2
torn.square 480 5
